  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved resilience of small farmers through increased access to market and adaptive practices</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to achieve improved livelihoods security for poor women, men and children from hazard-prone rural communities in southern part of Bangladesh through an integrated approach that increases the productivity and resilience of agricultural systems, strengthens engagement in markets and diversified income generation, and increases the ability of local producer groups to access services and influence development practices. Ulashi Sreejony Sangha (USS), based in Jessore will be working with small farmers in Jessore sadar, Jikorgacha and Monirampur Upazilas of Jessore district and Dacope upazila of Khulna district, in promoting greater crop production and increase market linkages and greater networking at nationally and cross border links.  This project will support a total of 1,300 (810 women and 490 men) multi-crop farmers and flower cultivators.</narrative>
  </description>
